English translation (for convenience; the Chinese text governs)

PREAMBLE. This work is a Traditional Chinese tutorial compilation, translation
and derived simulation experiments built around the MuJoCo physics engine and
its official documentation. The copyright holder wants it widely used,
discussed and shown, while keeping its commercial rights. This license is built
accordingly: non-commercial use is free and permissive; commercial use is
reserved for a separate agreement with the copyright holder.

1. DEFINITIONS.
   (a) "Work" means everything in this repository authored by the copyright
       holder, including tutorial documentation, translations and glossaries,
       example programs, modelling and verification tools, simulation models
       and meshes, experiment outputs (videos, trajectory logs, plots),
       trained policy weights, Contributions incorporated under Section 7,
       and compiled or packaged forms of any of these.
   (b) "Third-Party Materials" means the MuJoCo physics engine itself, the
       original text of its official documentation, and the third-party
       libraries, tools and datasets this repository depends on. They belong
       to Google DeepMind or their respective rights holders and are provided
       under their own licenses.
   (c) "Modified Version" means any work based on the Work through
       modification, translation, porting, extension or combination.
   (d) "Commercial Use" means use aimed at obtaining money or other
       consideration, directly or indirectly, including without limitation:
       selling the Work or a Modified Version; offering it for a fee, by
       subscription or membership; bundling it with goods, hardware or
       services; adding advertising, in-app purchases or sponsorship
       placements; using it in the operations, products or services of a
       for-profit entity; and using it in commercial exhibitions, events or
       marketing.
   (e) "Contribution" means anything intentionally submitted to the copyright
       holder for inclusion in the Work: code, documentation, translations,
       assets and proposed changes.

2. SCOPE AND EXCLUSIONS.
   (a) This license applies only to the Work.
   (b) This license does not apply to Third-Party Materials. The Work does not
       redistribute the MuJoCo engine or the original text of its
       documentation; users obtain those under the respective rights holders'
       terms (MuJoCo is under Apache License 2.0). The copyright holder claims
       no rights in Third-Party Materials and cannot license them.
   (c) For documentation, research and demonstration this repository contains
       small excerpts of Third-Party Materials: passages translated or
       summarised from the MuJoCo official documentation (Apache License 2.0),
       together with the API names, XML tags and parameter descriptions they
       contain. Those portions are outside this license and remain under the
       original rights holder's terms. Translations, rewrites and explanations
       authored by the copyright holder are part of the Work and are licensed
       under these terms to the extent of the copyright holder's rights in
       them; the translations are derivative of the original documentation and
       their use remains subject to the original license.
   (d) Third-party components in this repository or its packages (for example
       the MuJoCo, NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib, imageio, Gymnasium,
       Stable-Baselines3 and PyTorch Python packages)
       are provided under their own licenses, which are distributed with them,
       and are not governed by this license.

3. NON-COMMERCIAL GRANT. Subject to Section 5, anyone may, free of charge and
   without prior permission:
   (a) use, run, reproduce and distribute the Work for personal, educational,
       research, preservation, commentary or other non-commercial purposes;
   (b) make Modified Versions and distribute them under this license on the
       same non-commercial condition; whoever distributes a Modified Version
       agrees to license their own changes to others on the same terms as
       this license;
   (c) make translations or language packs and distribute them under this
       license on the same non-commercial condition.

4. EXPRESSLY PERMITTED SHOWCASE AND COVERAGE. The following are not
   Commercial Use under Section 1(d) even if they generate income, and are
   expressly permitted:
   (a) recording, streaming, broadcasting, reviewing, teaching or reporting
       on the Work or a Modified Version, including earning advertising
       revenue, viewer donations or membership income under the ordinary
       rules of platforms such as YouTube, Twitch or Bilibili;
   (b) quoting, showing or discussing the Work — including screenshots, code
       excerpts and documentation — in articles, books, academic papers,
       talks, exhibitions or courses;
   (c) showing or providing the Work at preservation, academic, non-profit or
       community events.
   Attribution under Section 5(b) applies. The following remain Commercial
   Use and are not covered by this Section: selling the Work or a Modified
   Version as the main object of sale; packaging it as a paid product or
   service; and using it as a marketing tool or demonstration content for
   other goods, hardware or services.

5. CONDITIONS.
   (a) Keep this license and the copyright notice in every distribution of
       the Work or a Modified Version.
   (b) When publicly distributing, showing or transmitting the Work or a
       Modified Version, give reasonable and visible credit: the name of the
       Work, the copyright holder (Wang Chun-Yu / wicanr2), and the original
       source at https://github.com/wicanr2/mujoco-tutorial-zh .
   (c) When distributing a Modified Version, state clearly that it is
       modified, what was changed and by whom. Do not imply that it comes
       from or is endorsed by the copyright holder, and do not use the
       copyright holder's name or the Work's name in a confusing way.
   (d) Do not charge for obtaining or using the Work or a Modified Version
       itself (actual cost of physical media and shipping excepted), and do
       not exchange them for other consideration. Income permitted by
       Section 4 is not restricted by this paragraph.
   (e) When distributing Third-Party Materials alongside the Work, comply with
       their own licenses and distribute their license notices with them.
   (f) Do not remove, obscure or alter copyright, license or attribution
